   "type": "Story",
   "description": "## User story\n\n**As a** fulfilment coordinator\n**I want** to search orders by date range **and** status\n**so that** I can see only the orders I need to act on (e.g. all `CONFIRMED` orders this week).\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n1. **Given** orders in several statuses, **when** I call\n   `GET /api/v1/orders?from=2026-01-01&to=2026-03-31&status=DELIVERED`,\n   **then** only `DELIVERED` orders in that range are returned.\n2. **Given** I don't pass `status`, **then** the behaviour is unchanged (all statuses).\n3. **Given** I pass several statuses `status=PENDING&status=CONFIRMED`, **then** orders in either status are returned.\n4. **Given** an unknown status `status=LOST`, **then** `400 Bad Request`.\n5. Swagger documentation shows the new parameter.\n\n## Out of scope\n\nFiltering by customer, sorting options.\n\n## Technical notes\n\n* Spring Data derived queries support `...AndStatusIn(Collection<OrderStatus> statuses, ...)`.\n* Update `docs/http/oms.http` and `CHANGELOG.md`.",
