   "type": "Story",
   "description": "## User story\n\n**As an** on-call engineer\n**I want** every request to carry a correlation ID that appears in all its log lines and in error\nresponses\n**so that** I can trace a customer complaint to the exact logs in seconds.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n1. If the request has an `X-Correlation-Id` header, that value is used; otherwise a UUID is generated.\n2. The ID is returned in the `X-Correlation-Id` response header for **every** response, including errors.\n3. Every log line written while handling the request includes the ID.\n4. Problem-detail error responses include a `correlationId` property.\n5. A header value longer than 64 chars or with characters outside `[A-Za-z0-9-]` is ignored\n   and a new ID generated (log-injection protection).\n6. The ID doesn't leak into the next request handled by the same thread.\n\n## Technical notes\n\n* Servlet `OncePerRequestFilter` + SLF4J `MDC`. Clean up in `finally`.\n* Update the logging pattern in `application.yml`.",
